<title>GERMANY: Germany to sell 500 mln DM oil in 1998-gvt sources.</title>
<headline>Germany to sell 500 mln DM oil in 1998-gvt sources.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>German government sources on Friday said Bonn expected to raise around 500 million marks in revenue next year from the sale of a part of its crude oil reserves.</p>
<p>Earlier, sources said Germany planned to sell its entire strategic reserves of 7.3 million tonnes by the end of 1999. The sale of the first tranche, of about 2.8 million barrels of oil, is expected in a few weeks, a source said earlier.</p>
<p>On Thursday, government sources said Bonn hoped to raise 400 million marks through such sales in 1997.</p>
<p>Chancellor Helmut Kohl's cabinet on Friday approved the plans to sell government crude oil reserves.</p>
<p>--Bonn Newsroom +49 228 26097160</p>
</text>
